cameras.description:
same filters and validation as `list_protect_events` (camera names resolve to IDs;
smart_detect_types without types is sent with a _warnings entry).
Shape: string|string[]

types.description:
same filters and validation as `list_protect_events` (camera names resolve to IDs;
smart_detect_types without types is sent with a _warnings entry).
Shape: string|string[]

threat_types.description:
Optional threat kinds to include, e.g. ["THREAT"] or ["HONEYPOT"];
default ["HONEYPOT", "THREAT"].
Shape: string[]

key_label.description:
Optional configured API-key label (see list_configured_api_keys) to read one
key. Omit it to cover every key. With several keys configured, page_token needs it;
without it the call fails listing the labels.

ports.description:
Ports to clear. Shape: {port_idx:integer,unit_id?:integer}[].
Each item names a port (unit_id for a stack member);
for example [{"port_idx": 5}].

policy.description:
Complete official firewall policy object. Fetch it with get_firewall_policy;
omitted optional fields are cleared by this PUT.
Advisory spec fields; any JSON passes. Required: action, destination, enabled, ipProtocolScope, loggingEnabled, name, source.

payload.description:
spec: free-form (Network v2 trafficroutes, snake_case). FULL replacement object;
start from get_traffic_route output.
Free-form JSON object; no fixed body shape is published.
